       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That's twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum per dose of 1,000 \u043a\u0438lo\u0433\u0440\u0430\u043c\u043c. At this level the risk of lactic acidosis is significant, even with normal renal function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day, the max\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg** per dose at a different frequency\n\nIf you want the original 1,700 mg TID order anyway, tell me and I'll enter it with a note that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away."
